{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfaJr2yfFbsmN1rYRM77S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 03 is done: Lengauer's Theorem 3 is proved in Lean with no `sorry`, and the gate passes (`lake build` ok, 1 `sorry` against a limit of 1, 1,256 tests passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n**What is proved** (in `lean/MOSPFormalization/Complex/Pebbling.lean`, imported from the root). The only axioms used are the standard three: `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`.\n- **The game.** The progressive black-white game is defined as in Lengauer: each vertex passes once through pebble-free, white, black and cleared. The moves are place white, turn black and remove black. G_d is `lengauerD G`, and I proved it has no directed path of length two, so it is a dag.\n- **The instance form:** `pebblesWithin_lengauerD_iff` says G_d can be pebbled with K + 2 pebbles if and only if vs(G) ≤ K, for every graph and every K ≥ 0, with no other hypothesis.\n- **Lengauer's own wording** (VSG positive ⇔ PBWP positive at K + 2) is `isPositiveVSG_iff_isPositivePBWP_lengauerD`, for every positive K.\n- **The number form:** when G has an edge, pbw(G_d) = vs + 2 = pw + 2 = VSG + 2 (`pbw_lengauerD` and its two variants). When G has no edges but at least one vertex, pbw(G_d) = 1 (`pbw_lengauerD_of_edgeless`). That is the edge case item 02 found.\n\n**The proof does not follow the plan from item 01.** That plan was Lengauer's route: his Theorem 2 applied to G_d, then his Theorem 4. The Lean proof works on G_d directly:\n- **Layout to pebbling:** clear the vertices in layout order. For each vertex, blacken its closed neighbourhood, pass a pebble through each of its edge vertices, then remove it.\n- **Pebbling to layout:** order the vertices by when they lose their pebble. At each cut, look at the moment the last edge crossing the cut turns black. That edge vertex, its endpoint on the cleared side, and every vertex on the other side's boundary are pebbled at once, which forces the +2.\n\nAs a result, Theorem 2 is still unproved and remains the work of item 04.\n\n**Python checks.** In `paper2/complex_check.py`, `python -m paper2.complex_check --pebbling-strategy` replays both of the proof's constructions under the Lean rules. It runs every layout of all 1,252 graphs on 1–7 vertices, 5,378,453 plays in 9 s, with zero failures. `tests/test_pebbling_check.py` has five new tests. One limit: the check of the pebbling-to-layout direction only runs on plays the strategy itself produces. The statement was checked against all plays in item 02, and the Lean proof covers every play.\n\n**Docs.**\n- `paper2/problem_transformations.md` gains problem §1.13, transformation (E10), and its proof in both the formal and the plain-English register.\n- `paper2/equivalences.md` gains section P.8, and row 13c is marked proved.\n- `paper2/axiom_check.lean` has the new theorems added.\n\nPROGRESS.md now reads 3/13 and item 03 is marked `[x]`. Nothing was committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":768,"cache_read_input_tokens":210090,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":768,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":825,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0421787-9928-43c9-9b6f-3633ca184b0d","uuid":"e5113ba7-7781-4dbb-8282-7d3e7ef97680","timestamp":"2026-09-30T21:09:15.117Z","request_id":"req_011CfaJr2XcwyNLGj6pAZejz"}
